{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-163583" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/2f847a5551c0bdc5aea20673814ba6eddc10daca7661cca2b2db76c953672225.png)\n\nA plate occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the $y$-axis and the lines $x=y-1$ and $x=7-y$, as shown above. The mass density function of the plate is $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{y-1}{9}.$ Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163583" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\,x+1\\le y\\le 7-x},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/b86b9a595786e544159e08fef12952c88e1bf9f796fb4ae3089e877dc9119b3f.png)\n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=3$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-3|\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{x+1}^{7-x}(\\frac{y-1}{9})|x-3{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{x+1}^{7-x}(\\frac{y-1}{9})(x-3)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(x-3)^{2}[{\\int }_{x+1}^{7-x}\\frac{y-1}{9}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(x-3)^{2}{[\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{18}]}_{x+1}^{7-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(x-3)^{2}[\\frac{(6-x)^{2}}{18}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{18}]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(x-3)^{2}[\\frac{12(3-x)}{18}]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(x-3)^{3}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}{[\\frac{(x-3)^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}(0-\\frac{81}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163583" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e00e282368dae98d9ea5aaf0a8e9459a5e55b02111a1d9b4eb713e83a11c3a4a"} {"question" "q-163583" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163583" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "29"] ["math" "30"] ["math" "\\frac{19}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{21}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{27}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163583" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{27}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163493" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A rectangular plate occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1}$\nwith mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=x+y-1$ Find the moment of inertia of this plate about the line $x=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163493" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-2|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+y-1)|x-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-2+y+1)(x-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-2)^{3}+(y+1)(x-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{[y(x-2)^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}(y+1)^{2}(x-2)^{2}]}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}(x-2)^{3}+\\frac{3}{2}(x-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{(x-2)^{4}}{4}+\\frac{(x-2)^{3}}{2}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{2})-(\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163493" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e00e282368dae98d9ea5aaf0a8e9459a5e55b02111a1d9b4eb713e83a11c3a4a"} {"question" "q-163493" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163493" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163493" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163501" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A rectangular plate occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 2}$\nwith mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=y-x.$ Find the moment of inertia of this plate about the line $x=-2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163501" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=-2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-(-2)|=|x+2|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=-2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(y-x)|x+2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(y-x)(x+2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}y(x+2)^{2}-x(x+2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}(x+2)^{2}-xy(x+2)^{2}]}_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{1}(3-2x)(x+2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{1}(-2{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+4x+12)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[\\frac{-{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{5{x}^{3}}{3}+2{x}^{2}+12x]}_{-2}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}((-\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{5}{3}+2+12)-(-8+\\frac{40}{3}+8-24)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}((14-\\frac{13}{6})-(-24+\\frac{40}{3})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{135}{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{45}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163501" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e00e282368dae98d9ea5aaf0a8e9459a5e55b02111a1d9b4eb713e83a11c3a4a"} {"question" "q-163501" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163501" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{15}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{21}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{31}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{45}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{70}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163501" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{45}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163563" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/74c26773d49442671fcf6526764215523ca0231a7889671330a7ac539f3402fc.png)\n\nA plate occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the $y$-axis and the lines $x=2y$ and $x=3-y$, as shown above. The mass density function of the plate is $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{y}{6}.$ Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163563" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,\\frac{x}{2}\\le y\\le 3-x},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/0c9efcbae53bdd2620b0bf7009ce4f4f2a20a38f393cac008899621ec391d261.png)\n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-2|\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{x/2}^{3-x}(\\frac{y}{6})|x-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{x/2}^{3-x}(\\frac{y}{6})(x-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{2}-4x+4)[{\\int }_{x/2}^{3-x}\\frac{y}{6}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{2}-4x+4){[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{12}]}_{x/2}^{3-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{2}-4x+4)[\\frac{(3-x)^{2}}{12}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{48}]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{48}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{2}-4x+4)(36-24x+3{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{48}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3{x}^{4}-36{x}^{3}+144{x}^{2}-240x+144\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{5}}{80}-\\frac{3{x}^{4}}{16}+{x}^{3}-\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{2}+3x]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{2}{5}-3+8-10+6)-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163563" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e00e282368dae98d9ea5aaf0a8e9459a5e55b02111a1d9b4eb713e83a11c3a4a"} {"question" "q-163563" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163563" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163563" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7}{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/55a781e535e1b469bc5da659eff8f82afd27a1e8bb92ccd36c2fce5a9dd49b07.png)\n\nA plate occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the $y$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{4y}{3}$ and $x=4-\\frac{4y}{3}$, as shown above. The mass density function of the plate is $\\lambda (x,y)=2-x.$ Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,\\frac{3}{4}x\\le y\\le 3-\\frac{3}{4}x},\n$$\n\n \n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/1f332ebf554ac0e1b9e5099244aa50de0beef38c92efcba04e95e73abd21ecb6.png)\n\n    \n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-2|\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{3x/4}^{3-3x/4}(2-x)|x-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{3x/4}^{3-3x/4}{(2-x)}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(2-x)^{3}[{\\int }_{3x/4}^{3-3x/4}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(2-x)^{3}[y]_{3x/4}^{3-3x/4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(2-x)^{3}(3-\\frac{3x}{4}-\\frac{3x}{4})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(2-x)^{4}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}{[\\frac{(2-x)^{5}}{5}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}(0-\\frac{{2}^{5}}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{48}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e00e282368dae98d9ea5aaf0a8e9459a5e55b02111a1d9b4eb713e83a11c3a4a"} {"question" "q-163568" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163568" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{28}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{32}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{33}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{36}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{48}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163568" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{48}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163000" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/ed4f595e7613254fd0cb8f27cf0b0f7443cfbe382ab525b0ca8d527c07f528fd.png)\n\nA plate with mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region $D$ enclosed between the curves $y={x}^{2}$ and $y=\\sqrt{x}$, as shown above. Given that the region has an area of $\\frac{1}{3},$ find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163000" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/60ec523346df73503dd61893994de6ec31069271b1157f153bbe988c9e694798.png)\n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=1$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-1|.\n$$\n\nSince the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=3M.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =3M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{\\sqrt{x}}|x-1{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{\\sqrt{x}}(x-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3M{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-1)^{2}[y]_{y={x}^{2}}^{y=\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3M{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}-2x+1)(\\sqrt{x}-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{5/2}-2{x}^{3/2}+{x}^{1/2}-{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3M{[\\frac{2}{7}{x}^{7/2}-\\frac{4}{5}{x}^{5/2}+\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2}-\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =3M(\\frac{2}{7}-\\frac{4}{5}+\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{3}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{5M}{14}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163000" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e00e282368dae98d9ea5aaf0a8e9459a5e55b02111a1d9b4eb713e83a11c3a4a"} {"question" "q-163000" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163000" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{4M}{7}"] ["math" "\\frac{5M}{14}"] ["math" "\\frac{5M}{7}"] ["math" "\\frac{8M}{7}"] ["math" "\\frac{9M}{14}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163000" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5M}{14}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163622" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}.$\nFind the moment of inertia of this plate about the line $x=-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163622" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, the distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=-1$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x+1|.\n$$\n\nNext, the area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=3\\cdot 2=6.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{M}{6}|x+1{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{M}{6}(x+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}({\\int }_{-1}^{2}(x+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}\\cdot [\\frac{1}{3}(x+1)^{3}]_{-1}^{2}\\cdot [y]_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}(\\frac{1}{3}(2+1)^{3}-\\frac{1}{3}(-1+1)^{3})\\cdot (2-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}(9-0)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3M.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163622" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e00e282368dae98d9ea5aaf0a8e9459a5e55b02111a1d9b4eb713e83a11c3a4a"} {"question" "q-163622" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163622" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2M"] ["math" "3M"] ["math" "4M"] ["math" "5M"] ["math" "M"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163622" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3M"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163621" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,2\\le x\\le 5,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 2}.$\nFind the moment of inertia of this plate about the line $x=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163621" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, the distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-2|.\n$$\n\nNext, the area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=3\\cdot 1=3.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\frac{M}{3}|x-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\frac{M}{3}(x-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}({\\int }_{2}^{5}(x-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}\\cdot [\\frac{1}{3}(x-2)^{3}]_{2}^{5}\\cdot {[y]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}(\\frac{1}{3}(5-2)^{3}-\\frac{1}{3}(2-2)^{3})\\cdot (2-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}(9-0)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =3M.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163621" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e00e282368dae98d9ea5aaf0a8e9459a5e55b02111a1d9b4eb713e83a11c3a4a"} {"question" "q-163621" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163621" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2M"] ["math" "3M"] ["math" "M"] ["math" "\\frac{5M}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{M}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163621" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3M"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163626" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/cd19503a1b72cd353cd2bacad0c187a1f83881d511b6ffcf0e99755ab9f682a9.png)\n\nA plate with mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region $D$ enclosed between the curves $y={x}^{3}$ and $y=x$, as shown above. Given that the region has an area of $\\frac{1}{4},$ find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163626" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,{x}^{3}\\le y\\le x},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/4463119c9f2ff0c1c658dd573add51a000cc50187e7dd59f39a40ba7c3abfce2.png)\n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=1$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-1|.\n$$\n\nSince the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=4M.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =4M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{x}|x-1{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{x}(x-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4M{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-1)^{2}[y]_{y={x}^{3}}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4M{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}-2x+1)(x-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4M{\\int }_{0}^{1}x-2{x}^{2}+2{x}^{4}-{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4M{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{2{x}^{5}}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{6}}{6}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =4M(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{2}{5}-\\frac{1}{6}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163626" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e00e282368dae98d9ea5aaf0a8e9459a5e55b02111a1d9b4eb713e83a11c3a4a"} {"question" "q-163626" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163626" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{3M}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{4M}{15}"] ["math" "\\frac{4M}{7}"] ["math" "\\frac{5M}{7}"] ["math" "\\frac{M}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163626" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4M}{15}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163618" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}.$\nFind the moment of inertia of this plate about the line $y=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163618" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, the distance between a point on $D$ and the line $y=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|y-2|.\n$$\n\nNext, the area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=2\\cdot 2=4.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $y=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{M}{4}|y-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{M}{4}(y-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}({\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{2}(y-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}\\cdot [x]_{-1}^{1}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{3}(y-2)^{3}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}(1-(-1))(\\frac{1}{3}(2-2)^{3}-\\frac{1}{3}(0-2)^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}(0-(-\\frac{8}{3})) \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163618" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e00e282368dae98d9ea5aaf0a8e9459a5e55b02111a1d9b4eb713e83a11c3a4a"} {"question" "q-163618" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163618" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2M}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{4M}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{5M}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{5M}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{M}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163618" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4M}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163008" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/b48e086ae0e94589d557eceb25b50af9deffdec442cfb7a4e559577bce899c40.png)\n\nA triangular plate with mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ enclosed between the $x$-axis and the lines $x=1$ and $y=2x.$\nThe mass density at each point is proportional to its distance from the $x$-axis. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=-2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163008" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2x},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/f040a5500a1415b8617300f34074bb16d895889354ed7e722dbd668a233daebb.png)\n\nAlso, the distance between a point and the line $x=-2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-(-2)|=|x+2|.\n$$\n\nNext, the mass density can be written as $\\lambda (x,y)=k|y|=ky,$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find the value of $k$ by integrating the mass density function over the plate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2x}ky\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2x}y\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}2{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k\\cdot {[\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=ky=\\frac{3M}{2}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=-2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2x}\\frac{3M}{2}y\\,|x+2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2x}\\frac{3M}{2}y(x+2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+2)^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{2x}y\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+2)^{2}{[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2{x}^{2}(x+2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2{x}^{4}+8{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}{[\\frac{2}{5}{x}^{5}+2{x}^{4}+\\frac{8}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}[\\frac{2}{5}+2+\\frac{8}{3}-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}[\\frac{76}{15}] \\\\  & =\\frac{38M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163008" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e00e282368dae98d9ea5aaf0a8e9459a5e55b02111a1d9b4eb713e83a11c3a4a"} {"question" "q-163008" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163008" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "7M"] ["math" "\\frac{27M}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{32M}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{38M}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{42M}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163008" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{38M}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163660" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1}.$\nThe mass density at each point is proportional to the square of its distance from the $x$-axis. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $y=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163660" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, the distance between a point and the line $y=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|y-2|.\n$$\n\nNext, the mass density can be written as $\\lambda (x,y)=k{y}^{2},$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find the value of $k$ by integrating the mass density function over the plate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}k{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k({\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =k\\cdot [x]_{-2}^{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{3}(2-(-2))(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4k}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=k{y}^{2}=\\frac{3M}{4}{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $y=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3M}{4}{y}^{2}|y-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3M}{4}{y}^{2}(y-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}({\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{4}-4{y}^{3}+4{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}\\cdot [x]_{-2}^{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{{y}^{5}}{5}-{y}^{4}+\\frac{4{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}\\cdot (2-(-2))\\cdot (\\frac{1}{5}-1+\\frac{4}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}\\cdot 4\\cdot \\frac{8}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{8M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163660" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e00e282368dae98d9ea5aaf0a8e9459a5e55b02111a1d9b4eb713e83a11c3a4a"} {"question" "q-163660" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163660" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{16M}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{24M}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{8M}{15}"] ["math" "\\frac{8M}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{8M}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163660" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{8M}{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163729" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/2e8eee199131d64b8772e15acb848030ac810cc96fd20b4f75005e5aab2770ed.png)\n\nA plate with mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ enclosed between the curves $y={x}^{2}$ and $y=4$ in the first quadrant.\nThe mass density at each point is proportional to its distance from the $y$-axis. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $y=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163729" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 2},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/f5a73161415455032a7fd2031dba8f1c56a7ccb40bf6dc3e4fa405a69aee74d8.png)\n\nAlso, the distance between a point and the line $y=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|y-2|.\n$$\n\nNext, the mass density can be written as $\\lambda (x,y)=k|x|=kx,$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find the value of $k$ by integrating the mass density function over the plate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{4}kx\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{2}x[y]_{{x}^{2}}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{2}x(4-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{2}(4x-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{[2{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =k(8-4) \\\\  & =4k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=kx=\\frac{M}{4}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $y=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{4}\\frac{M}{4}x\\cdot |y-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{4}\\frac{M}{4}x\\cdot (y-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}x{[\\frac{(y-2)^{3}}{3}]}_{{x}^{2}}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}x(\\frac{8}{3}-\\frac{({x}^{2}-2)^{3}}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{12}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(8x-x({x}^{2}-2)^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{12}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(-{x}^{7}+6{x}^{5}-12{x}^{3}+16)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{12}{[-\\frac{{x}^{8}}{8}+{x}^{6}-3{x}^{4}+16x]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{12}(-32+64-48+32) \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163729" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e00e282368dae98d9ea5aaf0a8e9459a5e55b02111a1d9b4eb713e83a11c3a4a"} {"question" "q-163729" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163729" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{3M}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{3M}{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{4M}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{8M}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{M}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163729" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4M}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/aaa08372caf804751c80d37af49d0b27394dfe20b6d2dba6868a7739b4062921.png)\n\nA plate with mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ enclosed between the lines $y=\\frac{x}{2},$ $y=x,$ and $x=1.$ \nThe mass density at each point is proportional to the square of its distance from the $y$-axis. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $y=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,\\frac{x}{2}\\le y\\le x},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/84ec89a3f4d786fe387b33aacc3de7c013866387354897f785ff69f9d65437ad.png)\n\nAlso, the distance between a point and the line $y=0$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|y|.\n$$\n\nNext, the mass density can be written as $\\lambda (x,y)=k{x}^{2},$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find the value of $k$ by integrating the mass density function over the plate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{x/2}^{x}k{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{x/2}^{x}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[{x}^{2}y]}_{x/2}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{3}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k\\cdot {[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{8}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=k{x}^{2}=8M{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $y=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{x/2}^{x}8M{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{x/2}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8M{\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{{x}^{5}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{24})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8M{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{7{x}^{5}}{24}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =M{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{7{x}^{5}}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =M{[\\frac{7{x}^{6}}{18}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{7M}{18}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e00e282368dae98d9ea5aaf0a8e9459a5e55b02111a1d9b4eb713e83a11c3a4a"} {"question" "q-163669" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163669" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{10M}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{28M}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{5M}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{7M}{18}"] ["math" "\\frac{7M}{9}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163669" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7M}{18}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163656" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3}.$\nThe mass density at each point is proportional to its $x$-coordinate. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $y=-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163656" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, the distance between a point and the line $y=-1$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|y+1|.\n$$\n\nNext, the mass density can be written as $\\lambda (x,y)=kx,$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find the value of $k$ by integrating the mass density function over the plate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}kx\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k({\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =k\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{2}\\cdot [y]_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =k(2-0)(3-0) \\\\  & =6k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=kx=\\frac{M}{6}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $y=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{M}{6}x|y+1{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{M}{6}x(y+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}({\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{3}(y+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{3}(y+1)^{3}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(4-0)\\cdot [\\frac{1}{3}(64-1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}\\cdot 2\\cdot \\frac{63}{3} \\\\  & =7M.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163656" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e00e282368dae98d9ea5aaf0a8e9459a5e55b02111a1d9b4eb713e83a11c3a4a"} {"question" "q-163656" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163656" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "7M"] ["math" "\\frac{64M}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{65M}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{65M}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{7M}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "q-163656" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7M"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb6015d7f2ad6f88d1ef663a457a8fd7d01f099f47e125f1bd76242a322cda1"} {"question" "e-12485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/0405639a97f249bbcc4dc18a7eae5b4df24aefb4b4680b569365b3d841c15e6b.png)\n\n   \n\nA plate occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the $y$-axis and the lines $x=\\dfrac{y}2$ and $x=y-2$, as shown above. The mass density function of the plate is $\\lambda(x,y) =\\dfrac y8.$ Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/example-12485.json" "file_sha256" "c2680f95bffff4a1fb2e7e562760afaaa000f8396a1f09392a719171ed503b16"} {"question" "e-12485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\nI_l = \\iint\\limits_D \\lambda (x,y) [r(x,y)]^2 \\:\\textrm{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda(x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 2, \\:\\: 2x \\leq y \\leq x+2 \\right\\},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/69dcf02cc1883f2b04f81bd6dd486bbe24fedbb813db5778ae3b33ed1fb42e90.png)\n\n     \n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y) = |x - 2|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{2x}^{x+2}(\\frac{y}{8})|x-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{2x}^{x+2}(\\frac{y}{8})(x-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(x-2)^{2}{\\int }_{2x}^{x+2}\\frac{y}{8}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(x-2)^{2}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}]}_{2x}^{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(x-2)^{2}((x+2)^{2}-(2x)^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{2}-4x+4)(4+4x-3{x}^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(16-24{x}^{2}+16{x}^{3}-3{x}^{4})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}{[16x-8{x}^{3}+4{x}^{4}-\\frac{3{x}^{5}}{5}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}(32-64+64-\\frac{96}{5})-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}(\\frac{64}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/example-12485.json" "file_sha256" "c2680f95bffff4a1fb2e7e562760afaaa000f8396a1f09392a719171ed503b16"} {"question" "e-12486" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/67d511da69c49e77822011936522f2b236ccc0fa0e0fcd09ce26b428cc8f738a.png)\n\n \n\nA plate with mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region $D$ enclosed between the curves $y=x$ and $y=4x-x^2$, as shown above. Given that the region has an area of $\\dfrac92$ square units, find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/example-12486.json" "file_sha256" "016bffbea125cae631c2da145cc4f5880f110fa51239cfd3a8a43502f3f616a5"} {"question" "e-12486" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\nI_l = \\iint\\limits_D \\lambda (x,y) [r(x,y)]^2 \\:\\textrm{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda(x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 3, \\:\\: x \\leq y \\leq 4x-x^2 \\right\\},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/6291950b5483f3c102df7249674412c7c11646409cb1b43df604de6bd5ace86f.png)\n\n  \n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=3$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y) = |x - 3|.\n$$\n\nSince the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda(x,y) = \\dfrac{M}{\\mathcal{A}} = \\dfrac{2M}{9}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{x}^{4x-{x}^{2}}|x-3{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{x}^{4x-{x}^{2}}(x-3)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(x-3)^{2}[y]_{y=x}^{y=4x-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}({x}^{2}-6x+9)(3x-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}-{x}^{4}+9{x}^{3}-27{x}^{2}+27x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{[-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}+\\frac{9{x}^{4}}{4}-9{x}^{3}+\\frac{27{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{{3}^{2}}(-\\frac{{3}^{5}}{5}+\\frac{{3}^{6}}{4}-{3}^{5}+\\frac{{3}^{5}}{2}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot {3}^{3}M(-\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{3}{4}-1+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{27M}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/example-12486.json" "file_sha256" "016bffbea125cae631c2da145cc4f5880f110fa51239cfd3a8a43502f3f616a5"} {"question" "e-12488" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/8ec9b8832f3286032413c4016e88a58a593dfd1b32164e219dc1c2e56e3b0b97.png)\n\nA plate with mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ in the first quadrant enclosed between the curve $y=\\sqrt x$ and the line $x=1,$ as shown above. \nThe mass density at each point is proportional to its distance from the $x$-axis. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/example-12488.json" "file_sha256" "0f1f09a4f9e8c3792b30006a44fbc9ebe6f271bfca7264612fa362d603fc5486"} {"question" "e-12488" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\nI_l = \\iint\\limits_D \\lambda (x,y) [r(x,y)]^2 \\:\\textrm{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda(x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq \\sqrt x \\right\\},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/assets/7faaecf39250dbdd1b92d789f6c217afe883c27533b563dae82ed82d228d9b4d.png)\n\nAlso, the distance between a point and the line $x=-1$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y) = |x-(-1)| = |x+1|.\n$$\n\nNext, the mass density can be written as $\\lambda(x,y) = k |y| = ky,$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find the value of $k$ by integrating the mass density function over the plate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}ky\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-0)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\lambda(x,y) = k y = 4M y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}4My\\,|x+1{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}4My(x+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4M{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+1)^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4M{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+1)^{2}{[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2M{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+1)^{2}(x-0)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2M{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2M{[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}+\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2M(\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =2M\\cdot \\frac{17}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{17M}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070210/example-12488.json" "file_sha256" "0f1f09a4f9e8c3792b30006a44fbc9ebe6f271bfca7264612fa362d603fc5486"}] "usage" {"e-12486" [] "e-12488" [] "q-163000" [] "q-163008" [] "e-12485" []} "basis" 2544 "retractions" [[17592186198575 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/4173/Source/Images/q-163000.png)\n\nA plate with mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region $D$ enclosed between the curves $y = x^{2}$ and $y = \\sqrt{x}$, as shown above. Given that the region has an area of $\\frac{1}{3}$, find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x = 1$."] [17592186198577 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/4173/Source/Images/q-163008.png)\n\nA triangular plate with mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ enclosed between the $x$-axis and the lines $x = 1$ and $y = 2x$.\nThe mass density at each point is proportional to its distance from the $x$-axis. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x =-2$."] [17592186197985 :question/problem "A plate occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the $y$-axis and the lines $x=\\dfrac{y}2$ and $x=y-2$, as shown above. The mass density function of the plate is $\\lambda(x,y) =\\dfrac y8$. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=2$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/4173/Source/Images/11eed00af0f2d1ea5c3dd9df00a40291.png)"] [17592186197985 :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\nI_l = \\iint\\limits_D \\lambda (x,y) [r(x,y)]^2 \\:\\textrm{d}A\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda(x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D$.\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 2, \\:\\: 2x \\leq y \\leq x+2 \\right\\}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/4173/Source/Images/3888077dfe4169493752346eb2247621.png)\n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y) = \\mid x - 2 \\mid\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI &= ∬_(D)λ(x, y)[r(x, y)]^{2}dA \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}∫_{2x}^{x + 2}(\\frac{y}{8}) \\mid x - 2 \\mid ^{2}dydx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}∫_{2x}^{x + 2}(\\frac{y}{8})(x - 2)^{2}dydx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}(x - 2)^{2}∫_{2x}^{x + 2}\\frac{y}{8}dydx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}(x - 2)^{2}[\\frac{y^{2}}{16}]_{2x}^{x + 2}dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{16}∫_{0}^{2}(x - 2)^{2}((x + 2)^{2} - (2x)^{2})dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{16}∫_{0}^{2}(x^{2} - 4x + 4)(4 + 4x - 3x^{2})dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{16}∫_{0}^{2}(16 - 24x^{2} + 16x^{3} - 3x^{4})dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{16}[16x - 8x^{3} + 4x^{4} - \\frac{3x^{5}}{5}]_{0}^{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{16}(32 - 64 + 64 - \\frac{96}{5}) - 0 \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{16}(\\frac{64}{5}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{4}{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186197986 :question/problem "A plate with mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region $D$ enclosed between the curves $y=x$ and $y=4x-x^2$, as shown above. Given that the region has an area of $\\dfrac92$ square units, find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=3$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/4173/Source/Images/b0b9a3962cb0c3c1dde403ebea8607ff.png)"] [17592186197986 :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\nI_l = \\iint\\limits_D \\lambda (x,y) [r(x,y)]^2 \\:\\textrm{d}A\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda(x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D$.\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 3, \\:\\: x \\leq y \\leq 4x-x^2 \\right\\}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/4173/Source/Images/03b423d9e4de7171ae11eedbfe4af11d.png)\n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=3$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y) = \\mid x - 3 \\mid\n$$\n\nSince the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda(x,y) = \\dfrac{M}{\\mathcal{A}} = \\dfrac{2M}{9}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI &= ∬_(D)λ(x, y)[r(x, y)]^{2}dA \\\\\n&= \\frac{2M}{9}∫_{0}^{3}∫_{x}^{4x - x^{2}} \\mid x - 3 \\mid ^{2}dydx \\\\\n&= \\frac{2M}{9}∫_{0}^{3}∫_{x}^{4x - x^{2}}(x - 3)^{2}dydx \\\\\n&= \\frac{2M}{9}∫_{0}^{3}(x - 3)^{2}[y]_{y = x}^{y = 4x - x^{2}}dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{2M}{9}∫_{0}^{3}(x^{2} - 6x + 9)(3x - x^{2})dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{2M}{9}∫_{0}^{3} - x^{4} + 9x^{3} - 27x^{2} + 27xdx \\\\\n&= \\frac{2M}{9}[- \\frac{x^{5}}{5} + \\frac{9x^{4}}{4} - 9x^{3} + \\frac{27x^{2}}{2}]_{0}^{3} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2M}{3^{2}}(-\\frac{3^{5}}{5} + \\frac{3^{6}}{4} - 3^{5} + \\frac{3^{5}}{2}) \\\\\n&= 2 \\cdot 3^{3}M(-\\frac{1}{5} + \\frac{3}{4} - 1 + \\frac{1}{2}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{27M}{10}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186197988 :question/problem "A plate with mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ in the first quadrant enclosed between the curve $y=\\sqrt x$ and the line $x=1$, as shown above.\nThe mass density at each point is proportional to its distance from the $x$-axis. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=-1$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/4173/Source/Images/edc9cb439dea888f2ce37f4d8ad17b5c.png)"] [17592186197988 :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\nI_l = \\iint\\limits_D \\lambda (x,y) [r(x,y)]^2 \\:\\textrm{d}A\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda(x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D$.\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq \\sqrt x \\right\\}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/4173/Source/Images/37d6c9a2f0b721457fa666b86f4e9c8d.png)\n\nAlso, the distance between a point and the line $x=-1$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y) = \\begin{vmatrix}x-(-1) & = & x+1\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nNext, the mass density can be written as\n\n$$\n\\lambda(x,y) = k \\mid y \\mid = ky\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find the value of $k$ by integrating the mass density function over the plate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nM &= ∬_(D)λ(x, y)dA \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}kydydx \\\\\n&= k∫_{0}^{1}[\\frac{1}{2}y^{2}]_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{k}{2}∫_{0}^{1}(x - 0)dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{k}{2}∫_{0}^{1}xdx \\\\\n&= \\frac{k}{2} \\cdot [\\frac{1}{2}x^{2}]_{0}^{1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{k}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\lambda(x,y) = k y = 4M y\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nI_{l} &= ∬_(D)λ(x, y)[r(x, y)]^{2}dA \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}4My \\mid x + 1 \\mid ^{2}dydx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}4My(x + 1)^{2}dydx \\\\\n&= 4M∫_{0}^{1}(x + 1)^{2}∫_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}ydydx \\\\\n&= 4M∫_{0}^{1}(x + 1)^{2}[\\frac{1}{2}y^{2}]_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}dx \\\\\n&= 2M∫_{0}^{1}(x + 1)^{2}(x - 0)dx \\\\\n&= 2M∫_{0}^{1}(x^{3} + 2x^{2} + x)dx \\\\\n&= 2M[\\frac{1}{4}x^{4} + \\frac{2}{3}x^{3} + \\frac{1}{2}x^{2}]_{0}^{1} \\\\\n&= 2M(\\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{2}{3} + \\frac{1}{2}) \\\\\n&= 2M \\cdot \\frac{17}{12} \\\\\n&= \\frac{17M}{6}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186194352 17592186194353 17592186194354 17592186194355 17592186194356 17592186194364 17592186194365 17592186194366 17592186194367 17592186194368] "immutable_fields" [[17592186194351 :answer-field/correct] [17592186194351 :answer-field/id] [17592186194351 :answer-field/key] [17592186194351 :answer-field/type] [17592186194363 :answer-field/correct] [17592186194363 :answer-field/id] [17592186194363 :answer-field/key] [17592186194363 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
